"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute top-0 left-0 w-3 h-3 border-t border-l border-[#F0D060]/40\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute top-0 right-0 w-3 h-3 border-t border-r border-[#C8AA6E]/30\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute bottom-0 left-0 w-3 h-3 border-b border-l border-[#C8AA6E]/30\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute bottom-0 right-0 w-3 h-3 border-b border-r border-[#C8AA6E]/30\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute -top-32 -right-24 w-72 h-72 rounded-full bg-[#C8AA6E]/[0.05] blur-3xl pointer-events-none\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative hero-article-body max-w-[860px] mx-auto\",\"children\":[[[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"When the draft actually belongs to the Monkey King\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"Patch 2.2.16 (\",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/patch-notes\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"patch notes\"}],\") was aimed at roaming Sun: Moonton said it trimmed that build for draining too many resources from its teammates, with minimal effect expected on the other lanes. Two side-lane effects reach you anyway. A killed Doppelganger pays the enemy far less gold, so clearing your bodies is a worse bargain for them, and the passive heals less on every clone hit, so do not count on clone chip to out-sustain the lane. He is a pressure pick, not a lane bully. If you draft him like a normal bruiser who must control every early skirmish, you are giving away the one edge he actually offers.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Pick Sun when the enemy composition has to answer side lanes with single-target damage or delayed rotations. He is at his best into drafts that only have one reliable AoE answer, especially if that answer is the mid laner. He also gets better when your own mid and roam can hold a 4v4 without begging for you to hard front-line.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The traps are consistent. X.Borg keeps tagging every body you make. Ruby resets short trades and drags you back in. Paquito and Phoveus are also bad signs because they either burst the real body early or punish your movement pattern. If the enemy already shows two of those answers, Sun stops being a clever lane pressure pick and becomes a tax on your own draft.\"}],\"\\n\",\"$L7e\",\"\\n\",\"$L7f\",\"\\n\",\"$L80\",\"\\n\",\"$L81\",\"\\n\",\"$L82\",\"\\n\",\"$L83\",\"\\n\",\"$L84\",\"\\n\",\"$L85\",\"\\n\",\"$L86\",\"\\n\",\"$L87\",\"\\n\",\"$L88\",\"\\n\",\"$L89\",\"\\n\",\"$L8a\",\"\\n\",\"$L8b\",\"\\n\",\"$L8c\",\"\\n\",\"$L8d\",\"\\n\",\"$L8e\"],\"$L8f\",\"$L90\"],\"$L91\"]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a7:I[392015,[\"$7\",\"$8\",\"$9\",\"$a\",\"$b\",\"$2e\",\"$3e\",\"$3f\"],\"default\"]\nb7:I[131354,[\"$7\",\"$8\",\"$9\",\"$a\",\"$b\",\"$2e\",\"$3e\",\"$3f\"],\"default\"]\n6d:[\"$\",\"$L6a\",\"benedetta\",{\"href\":\"/heroes/benedetta\",\"className\":\"group block\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxShadow\":\"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\